    {
      "id": "seg:paragraph:discussion:0011:0001",
      "blockId": "paragraph:discussion:0011",
      "type": "sentence",
      "source": "In this example, the [`assign(to:on:)`](publisher/assign(to:on:).md) sets the value of the `anInt` property on an instance of `MyClass`:",
      "normalizedSource": "In this example, the [`assign(to:on:)`](publisher/assign(to:on:).md) sets the value of the `anInt` property on an instance of `MyClass`:",
      "sourceHash": "918d598bb35e1c3dca5a75919f419bf567f6410aec7eb56c04faf3870c572028",
      "translatable": true,
      "contextBefore": "Use the [`assign(to:on:)`](publisher/assign(to:on:).md) subscriber when you want to set a given property each time a publisher produces a value.",
      "contextAfter": "```swift\nclass MyClass {\n    var anInt: Int = 0 {\n        didSet {\n            print(\"anInt was set to: \\(anInt)\", terminator: \"; \")\n        }\n    }\n}\n\nvar myObject = MyClass()\nlet myRange = (0...2)\ncancellable = myRange.publisher\n    .assign(to: \\.anInt, on: myObject)\n\n// Prints: \"anInt was set to: 0; anInt was set to: 1; anInt was set to: 2\"\n```",
      "documentTitle": "assign(to:on:)",
      "framework": "Combine",
      "ko": "",
      "status": "failed",
      "reviewed": false,
      "locked": false
    },
    {
      "id": "seg:code:discussion:0012:0001",
      "blockId": "code:discussion:0012",
      "type": "preserve",
      "source": "```swift\nclass MyClass {\n    var anInt: Int = 0 {\n        didSet {\n            print(\"anInt was set to: \\(anInt)\", terminator: \"; \")\n        }\n    }\n}\n\nvar myObject = MyClass()\nlet myRange = (0...2)\ncancellable = myRange.publisher\n    .assign(to: \\.anInt, on: myObject)\n\n// Prints: \"anInt was set to: 0; anInt was set to: 1; anInt was set to: 2\"\n```",
      "normalizedSource": "```swift class MyClass { var anInt: Int = 0 { didSet { print(\"anInt was set to: \\(anInt)\", terminator: \"; \") } } } var myObject = MyClass() let myRange = (0...2) cancellable = myRange.publisher .assign(to: \\.anInt, on: myObject) // Prints: \"anInt was set to: 0; anInt was set to: 1; anInt was set to: 2\" ```",
      "sourceHash": "d77394d5130fae8e3e03b55f34cc85e88bf311b2a3dd34f6666f86833a2213cb",
      "translatable": false,
      "preserveReason": "code",
      "contextBefore": "In this example, the [`assign(to:on:)`](publisher/assign(to:on:).md) sets the value of the `anInt` property on an instance of `MyClass`:",
      "contextAfter": "❗ **Important**: The [`Subscribers.Assign`](subscribers/assign.md) instance created by this operator maintains a strong reference to `object`, and sets it to `nil` when the upstream publisher completes (either normally or with an error).",
      "documentTitle": "assign(to:on:)",
      "framework": "Combine",
      "ko": "```swift\nclass MyClass {\n    var anInt: Int = 0 {\n        didSet {\n            print(\"anInt was set to: \\(anInt)\", terminator: \"; \")\n        }\n    }\n}\n\nvar myObject = MyClass()\nlet myRange = (0...2)\ncancellable = myRange.publisher\n    .assign(to: \\.anInt, on: myObject)\n\n// Prints: \"anInt was set to: 0; anInt was set to: 1; anInt was set to: 2\"\n```",
      "status": "preserved",
      "reviewed": false,
      "locked": true
