      "source": "❗ **Important**: The [`Subscribers.Assign`](subscribers/assign.md) instance created by this operator maintains a strong reference to `object`, and sets it to `nil` when the upstream publisher completes (either normally or with an error).",
      "normalizedSource": "❗ **Important**: The [`Subscribers.Assign`](subscribers/assign.md) instance created by this operator maintains a strong reference to `object`, and sets it to `nil` when the upstream publisher completes (either normally or with an error).",
      "sourceHash": "4d33e4efd77cc3c2de9b4cb7c624cb29890d095e48f943d92083e0a84dd67fa6",
      "translatable": true,
      "contextBefore": "```swift\nclass MyClass {\n    var anInt: Int = 0 {\n        didSet {\n            print(\"anInt was set to: \\(anInt)\", terminator: \"; \")\n        }\n    }\n}\n\nvar myObject = MyClass()\nlet myRange = (0...2)\ncancellable = myRange.publisher\n    .assign(to: \\.anInt, on: myObject)\n\n// Prints: \"anInt was set to: 0; anInt was set to: 1; anInt was set to: 2\"\n```",
